[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2521680101","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99504#issuecomment-2521680101","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99504","id":2521680101,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WTcjl","user":{"login":"LunaCapra","id":50772474,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzcyNDc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50772474?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra","html_url":"https://github.com/LunaCapra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-05T23:08:02Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T23:08:02Z","body":"I've added the same tag reading functionality to WAV in addition to Ogg Vorbis.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2521680101/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523198700","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99504#issuecomment-2523198700","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99504","id":2523198700,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WZPTs","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T12:59:02Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T12:59:02Z","body":"I've worked with [taglib](https://taglib.org) in the past when creating audio programs. Taglib abstracts over audio file tags and would be usable for all audio files, instead of needing to implement for each separately. If we're already using libraries to read the audio itself, though idk if it would actually save effort or tears in the long run. Any thoughts?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523198700/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523295037","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99504#issuecomment-2523295037","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99504","id":2523295037,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WZm09","user":{"login":"LunaCapra","id":50772474,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzcyNDc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50772474?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra","html_url":"https://github.com/LunaCapra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T13:48:55Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T13:48:55Z","body":"> I've worked with [taglib](https://taglib.org) in the past when creating audio programs. Taglib abstracts over audio file tags and would be usable for all audio files, instead of needing to implement for each separately. If we're already using libraries to read the audio itself, though idk if it would actually save effort or tears in the long run. Any thoughts?\r\n\r\nFor OGG Vorbis the comments were already being read with libvorbis but discarded.\r\nFor WAV the chunks were also already being read but no check for a LIST/INFO chunk was in place.\r\n\r\nSo in those cases I'm not so sure if using another library would be helpful but for a future implementation for ID3 tags it might be.\r\nI'm also not sure how ideal it would be to have a library that supports many more formats than godot supports out of the box.\r\n\r\nOverall though, if an implementation with a library instead of this manual approach is preferred, I would not mind this PR being superseded.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523295037/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2524199743","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99504#issuecomment-2524199743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99504","id":2524199743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WdDs_","user":{"login":"LunaCapra","id":50772474,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzcyNDc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50772474?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra","html_url":"https://github.com/LunaCapra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T21:23:36Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T21:27:38Z","body":"I believe the WAV oddities are an issue with (a lack of) standardization regarding how WAV files can incorporate metadata.\r\nFrom what I've read they do not have a general way to support metadata, it's just very common to include a RIFF chunk of type LIST with the list identifier of INFO ([See here](https://www.recordingblogs.com/wiki/list-chunk-of-a-wave-file)).\r\nFor example, Audacity does this.\r\n\r\n> Interestingly, \"ID3\" is the name of a metadata standard. Does that mean metadata is put before the RIFF file header in some WAV files?\r\n\r\nNothing stops anyone from including a different chunk (e.g. ID3) anywhere in the WAV file and depending on the version they can come at the very beginning of the file, however this kind of file will fail to load even without the PR.\r\n\r\n> [01 - Title Theme (Main Menu).zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18042497/01.-.Title.Theme.Main.Menu.zip)\r\n> Dolphin can read all the tags successfully, including an embedded cover:\r\n\r\nThis file seems to have both an ID3 chunk as well as an INFO chunk so Dolphin is likely reading the ID3 data instead.\r\n\r\nIf full handling of all kinds of WAV metadata is desired I would like to leave that to someone else, as that's beyond my scope of knowledge.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2524199743/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2741715879","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99504#issuecomment-2741715879","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99504","id":2741715879,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ja0On","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptio